  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Casting the card again due to rebound's delayed triggered ability is optional. If you choose not to cast the card, or if you can't (perhaps because there are no legal targets available), the card will stay exiled. You won't get another chance to cast it on a future turn. If you do cast the card, it's put into its owner's graveyard as normal once it resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "0fd57894-b917-41c8-a394-360d1d31b236",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell with rebound that you cast from your hand is countered or doesn't resolve (most likely because its targets have become illegal), none of its effects will happen, including rebound. The spell will be put into its owner's graveyard and you won't get to cast it again on your next turn.",
      "oracle_id": "0fd57894-b917-41c8-a394-360d1d31b236",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "0fd57894-b917-41c8-a394-360d1d31b236",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled creature returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled creature will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled creature will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creature will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "0fd57894-b917-41c8-a394-360d1d31b236",
      "published_at": "2019-06-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose the color when the ability resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "9603e553-f72d-40bf-94ab-596afb7d6db3",
      "published_at": "2013-01-24",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "After a spell with split second resolves (or otherwise leaves the stack), players may again cast spells and activate abilities before the next object on the stack resolves.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Casting a spell with split second won't affect spells and abilities that are already on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the resolution of a triggered ability involves casting a spell, that spell can't be cast if a spell with split second is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players may turn face-down creatures face up while a spell with split second is on the stack.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players still get priority while a card with split second is on the stack; their options are just limited to mana abilities and certain special actions.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Split second doesn't stop triggered abilities from triggering, such as that of Chalice of the Void. If one does, its controller puts it on the stack and chooses targets for it, if any. Those abilities will resolve as normal.",
      "oracle_id": "b80d2841-03b0-42d3-ac9b-51e793b1dc24",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
